      "costUsd": 0.007433,
      "pronunciationText": "This is the normal probability density function, and each part has a job. The power of e is minus the squared distance from the mean, over two sigma squared. The same distance either side squares to the same value, so the curve is symmetric. Further out, the power gets more negative, so the curve drops towards zero. But e to any power is positive, so it never reaches the axis. The number in front makes the total area exactly one. For the apples, two sigma squared is four hundred and fifty."
