      "pronunciationText": "Where's the highest point? By the chain rule, f prime of x is the derivative of the power, times f of x itself. Since f of x is always positive, the sign of the gradient comes from minus x minus mu. Left of the mean the gradient is positive, so the curve rises. Right of the mean it's negative, so the curve falls. It rises all the way to mu and falls all the way after, so x equals mu is the global maximum, not just ay local one. Its height is one over sigma root two pi."
