      "outputTokens": 776,
      "costUsd": 0.0070355,
      "pronunciationText": "Is that just these apples? Try last video's chip bags, with mean one seventy-five grams and standard deviation four. From one seventy-one to one seventy-nine, the calculator gives zero point six eight two seven again. Here's why. Changing mu slides the bell along. Changing sigma stretches it sideways and squashes it down by the same factor, so the area between matching marks doesn't change. Measured in sigmas from the mean, every normal curve is the same curve."
