      "inputTokens": 114,
      "outputTokens": 879,
      "costUsd": 0.007968,
      "pronunciationText": "That's the empirical rule. For any normal distribution, approximately sixty-eight percent of the data lie within one standard deviation of the mean, approximately ninety-five percent within two, and approximately ninety-nine point seven percent within three. They're approximate, because the calculator gave sixty-eight point two seven, and so on. Symmetry gives the tails. Outside one sigma is thirty-two percent, so sixteen percent in each tail. Outside two sigma, two and a half percent each side. Outside three sigma, zero point one five percent each side."
