      "pronunciationText": "The second number is the variance, so sigma is six. Sixty-eight and ninety-two are twelve either side of eighty, which is two sigma. So that probability is about ninety-five percent. Eighty-six is one sigma above. Outside one sigma is thirty-two percent, and half of that is above, so about sixteen percent. Thirty-two percent is wrong. That counts both tails."
