      "pronunciationText": "Match it to the general formula. The mean is forty, and the number in front has five where sigma goes, so sigma is five. The global maximum is at x equals forty, with height one over five root two pi. The points of inflection are one sigma either side, at thirty-five and forty-five. Forty plus or minus root fifty is wrong. Fifty is two sigma squared, not sigma squared."
